# posixutils-rs follows the DESCRIPTION less closely. Checked on samples of each class, none is a
# difference on a permission bit that the grammar defines:
# - a permcopy (u, g, o) is ignored or used wrongly (+u, g+u, a-g, a+u, u=g, ...);
# - "=" with a who clears the set-ID bits of the other classes (u=rwx,go= clears the setgid bit of a
#   directory, g= and o= the setuid bit of a file), and the sticky bit with u, g or o is set, which is
#   unspecified;
# - an octal mode keeps the set-ID and sticky bits of a directory (implementation-defined);
# - it accepts an empty clause and "" as a mode (",", "u+x,"), which are not in the grammar;
# - repeated options and options after the mode or the "--" operands are errors there (clap), ours takes
#   them as the Utility Syntax Guidelines say.
-- -u f0 f4 f6 f7 f77 fs fg d0 d7 dt dg
-R -R 755 f6
-R 0 d7
-R 000 tree
-R a-r tree
-R a-x tree
-R o+t dt dg
-R u-x tree
-R u=rwx d0 d7 dt dg
-RR 755 f6
, f0 f4 f6 f7 f77 fs fg d0 d7 dt dg
,, f0 f4 f6 f7 f77 fs fg d0 d7 dt dg
,u+x f0 f4 f6 f7 f77 fs fg d0 d7 dt dg
